connection sftp – SFTP
A server for file transfer over SSH

Fields (with:):
  host        Name or address of the server
              string, required, e.g. sftp.example.com
  port        TCP port; empty: 22
              string, e.g. 22
  hostKey     Fingerprint of the host key as ssh-keygen -l shows it, e.g. SHA256:…; several separated by spaces. Without it Runnel does not connect and names the fingerprint of the server to check
              string, e.g. SHA256:ExampleFingerprintOfTheServerHostKeyAbcdefg
  user        User name for the sign-in
              string, required, e.g. runnel
  password    Password of the user; use ${secret:NAME}
              string
  privateKey  Private key in PEM format (OpenSSH, PKCS#1 or PKCS#8), instead of or together with password; use ${secret:NAME}
              string
  passphrase  Passphrase of a protected privateKey; use ${secret:NAME}
              string
  timeout     Longest time to connect and sign in
              string, duration, default 15s

Errors:
  Fails without hostKey, naming the fingerprint of the server to check with its administrator, and when the host key does not match hostKey; Runnel never trusts a host key on first use. Also fails when the server does not answer within timeout, the sign-in is refused (user, password or key), neither password nor privateKey is set, privateKey is no PEM key or needs passphrase, or the server offers no SFTP.

Test connection:
  Connects, checks the host key against hostKey, signs in and lists the start folder; without hostKey it names the fingerprint of the server. Nothing is written.

Example (connections/<name>.yaml):
  kind: Connection
  apiVersion: runnel/v1
  name: partner-sftp
  description: SFTP server of the partner
  type: sftp
  with:
    host: sftp.example.com
    hostKey: SHA256:ExampleFingerprintOfTheServerHostKeyAbcdefg
    user: runnel
    privateKey: ${secret:partner-sftp-key}
